cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Barye: physical simulation from many cooperating local solvers"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Barye splits a physical simulation into many small patches. Each patch is
  advanced by its own local solver, classical or learned, and patches
  cooperate only by exchanging values at their borders. It runs on ordinary
  CPU cores without a GPU and builds on the crates of Dyne, which runs the
  same scheme on microcontrollers, so the same patch solvers can run on both.
  Results are checked bit for bit against the single-patch solution.
authors:
  - family-names: "Koyabu"
    given-names: "Natsuhi"
repository-code: "https://github.com/physical-edge-native/barye"
# No version or release date until the first release (they are added then, together with the DOI).
# Barye is dual licensed: MIT OR Apache-2.0, at your option (see LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE).
# Zenodo's GitHub integration accepts only a single SPDX identifier here (a list makes the
# metadata import fail), so the Apache-2.0 half is declared. The MIT option still applies.
license: "Apache-2.0"
keywords:
  - numerical simulation
  - domain decomposition
  - partial differential equations
  - WebAssembly
  - physics-informed neural networks
